  "question": {
    "text": "If the A.M. between $p^{\\text {th }}$ and $q^{\\text {th }}$ terms of an A.P. is equal to the A.M. between $r^{\\text {th }}$ and $s^{\\text {th }}$ terms of the same A.P., then $p+q$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "bYRWS",
      "text": "\n$r+s-1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vfNR1",
      "text": "\n$r+s-2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3VJBU",
      "text": "\n$r+s+1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "cChJt",
      "text": "\n$r+s$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given: $\\frac{a_p+a_q}{2}=\\frac{a_r+a_s}{2}$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow a+(p-1) d+a+(q-1) d \\\\\n& \\quad=a+(r-1) d+a+(s-1) d \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow 2 a+(p+q) d-2 d=2 a+(r+s) d-2 d \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow(p+q) d=(r+s) d \\Rightarrow p+q=r+s .\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
